      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "An unusual electrocardiogram was sent to Dr. J. Willis Hurst, who had no knowledge of the clinical details. Afterward, the clinical and laboratory findings were presented for his further comments. In conclusion, the case illustrates how much information can be gathered from just a 12-lead electrocardiogram when analyzed by an 87-year-old expert who continues to teach daily the skills of electrocardiography."},
